  "body": "MAINLINE-024, the P3 film. QUESTIONABLE. Not a certification.\n\nThe pillow radius is the 2.04 m bay, because the 011b formula is p = 2*sigma*t/s. Cap rise is 0.374346974907 m. The arc line load is 97370.0546722 N/m. At the pinned 80 um the stress is 1217125683.4 Pa. The own scan reproduces least factor 1.22552794688, global, at s 2.04 m.\n\nKapton HN at half of 231 MPa is 0.000843030776382 m and 1504.3248789 kg. Teonex Q51 at half of 210 MPa is 1584.83804143 kg. Both exist as films. Kapton oxygen is 0.00404221907772 kg/day and nitrogen is 0.0031593001418 kg/day. The scaled water row is 2.01233463886 kg/day and is not a hull humidity. The 016 allowance is 48.8944215019 kg/day. The 150 to 400 kg pump holds those sourced loads. No getter was opened.\n\nThe lightest design row is Zylon HM as a 0/90 filament at 60 percent of break, a Toyobo extrapolation of about 19 years. Mass 109.701010474 kg, 0.0872972903957 kg/m2. It is not a sourced film, resin is omitted, and a barrier is still required. Metallised 12 um Mylar passes 0.000177008068742 kg/day of oxygen. Nitrogen is not on that sheet. The structure alone is above 97.515 kg.\n\nThat mass restates the k 0.2 least factor to 1.15909090909, film, second global, at s 1.76 m. The Kapton mass restates it to 0.818028264063, global, at s 2.48 m. CNT sheet and graphene laminate have no opened allowable. PROJECTION. The brief names no next job.",
